2026-03-23 08:25:07,521 DEBUG redis-pub-sub-vs-streams description: Most engineers reach for Redis Pub/Sub out of habit, but its fire-and-forget semantics silently drop messages for offline consumers — a subtle reliability gap that only surfaces under failure conditions. This post cuts through the surface-level comparison to focus on the architectural decision point: when eventual delivery guarantees, consumer groups, and replay semantics in Streams justify the added operational complexity over Pub/Sub's simplicity. The key takeaway is a concrete decision framework based on consumer lifecycle, durability requirements, and fan-out patterns — so you pick the right primitive before you're debugging lost messages in production.
